40:**Motor drive and recording light (sheet 7).** MOTOR (F6) through R61 100 ohm to the gate of Q1, R62 100 kohm gate to ground, Q1 source to ground, drain MOTOR_DRV; D1 cathode on VDD_3V0, anode on MOTOR_DRV. M1 is on the band sheet. Light (W5): VDD_3V0, R41 680 ohm, LED1, drain of Q2; Q2 source to ground, gate on VDD_MIC. No chip pin touches the light.
42:**Band (sheet 8, new).** J_BAND_A (flex tail on the thumb side, 6 pads): 1 JOY_UP, 2 JOY_DOWN, 3 JOY_LEFT, 4 JOY_RIGHT, 5 BTN_REC, 6 GND. J_BAND_B (other tail, 9 pads): 1 MOT- (MOTOR_DRV), 2 MOT+ (VDD_3V0), 3 CELL+ (VBAT), 4 CELL- (GND), 5 NTC, 6 VBUS, 7 D- (USB_DN), 8 D+ (USB_DP), 9 GND. Behind them: SW1 UP, SW3 DOWN, SW4 LEFT, SW5 RIGHT and SW2 record, each one SKTAAAE010 with terminal P1 on its line and P2 on ground; M1 VC0720B088L, + on VDD_3V0, - on MOTOR_DRV; BT1 the curved cell, + on VBAT, - on ground; RT1 10 kohm NTC from NTC to ground, in the band at the cell; CP1 to CP4 the charging pads, VBUS, D-, D+, GND in order from -Y to +Y (case design, lead 2026-11-10). The pad order and pad numbers of the two tails are this schematic's own definition (not a maker pin).
